WHAT THIS FILE ESTABLISHES

  Whether the eleven classes that sql/connect/shims ships as client-only stubs are
  represented in THE GRAPH THIS RUN LOADED by their real implementations or by those
  stubs. AAP 0.5.1 prescribes exactly this route for a duplicate-class collision that
  bears on a conclusion: query the graph for the class and report what is there,
  rather than infer a winner from the frontend's output, which is not possible.

  It replaces a citation that had gone stale. An earlier lane measured this against a
  narrowed graph built over one primary artifact per module, which INCLUDED the shims
  archive; that graph does not exist in this generation and no substitute for the
  mandated graph is presented, so its stub-side counts are neither re-measured here
  nor restated as this generation's. What follows is measured first-hand against the
  graph every stage of this run loaded.

