  VERDICT: every one of the eleven carries its REAL implementation. The graph this run
  loaded was built over an input set that EXCLUDES both shims archives - sql/connect/shims
  is one of the seven reactor JAR projects absent from it - so no stub displaced anything,
  and no conclusion drawn from this graph is answered by a stub.

  The typeDecls column is 2 for ten of the eleven and 1 for the eleventh. Two declarations
  under one full name is the ordinary shape here rather than a collision: the frontend emits
  a type declaration alongside its companion/parent representation. The method counts are
  taken across the declarations that full name resolves to, which is what the question asks.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT ESTABLISH
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  ESTABLISHES : the graph in use is free of the stub-displacement hazard, measured per class.
  DOES NOT    : a winner map. This states what the graph contains, not which archive the
                frontend read last, and it is measured for these eleven classes only.
  DOES NOT    : anything about a graph containing the shims archive. The mandated graph over
                every JAR the build produced WOULD contain it, so the hazard is a named
                forward cost of that unmet requirement (D1) rather than a fact about this graph.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE QUERY, VERBATIM
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  // Measures, in the graph every stage of this run loaded, the method count of each class
  // that sql/connect/shims ships as a client-only stub. The graph's input set EXCLUDES both
  // shims archives, so these counts establish whether the real implementations are present.
  val names = List(
    "org.apache.spark.SparkConf",
    "org.apache.spark.SparkContext",
    "org.apache.spark.rdd.RDD",
    "org.apache.spark.api.java.JavaRDD",
    "org.apache.spark.sql.ExperimentalMethods",
    "org.apache.spark.sql.SparkSessionExtensions",
    "org.apache.spark.sql.execution.QueryExecution",
    "org.apache.spark.sql.internal.SessionState",
    "org.apache.spark.sql.internal.SharedState",
    "org.apache.spark.sql.sources.BaseRelation",
    "org.apache.spark.sql.util.ExecutionListenerManager")
  importCpg("/opt/blitzy-harness/cpg/spark.cpg")
  println("MEASURED-GRAPH-METHODS " + cpg.method.size)
  names.foreach { n =>
    val tds = cpg.typeDecl.fullNameExact(n).l
    val decls = tds.size
    val methods = tds.flatMap(_.method).size
    println(f"SHIMSCLASS\t$n\tdecls=$decls\tmethods=$methods")
  }
  println("SHIMS-PROBE-COMPLETE")

